// background_execution — a Global executes during a Stay window
// NOTE: external sub-opcode 1 ("external register write") is the cross-Formation
// convention (Chapter 2 §2.7); its meaning is supplied by a Formation. This
// example is illustrative — on the bare Core it drives the external-operation bus
// (ext_op_valid + subopcode/sub_operand/data) for one clock.
// State table:
//   0: Global Stay Set            (open the Stay window)
//   1: Global external sub-op 1, sub_operand=0x10, data=0xABCD
//        -> background-executed register write (D8-D15=addr, D16-D31=data)
//   2: Stay 100, timing_signals = 0x0001  (the wait that hosts the background op)
//   3: Global Reset (repeat)
00000200
ABCD1010
00010641
00000000
